From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: the laser event carries its ring texture set

V4's rings are drawn from a named texture set (<ringtextureset>, "ring"
unless a mod says otherwise), which the renderer resolves to a layer of the
particle atlas it already builds. The name travels in the `texture` field the
explosion events already use for the same purpose, and which a beam had
never filled in.

One field; no game logic.

---
diff --git a/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp b/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
--- a/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
@@ -213,6 +213,11 @@
 		// V4: the weapon's <totaltime>, which is what the client body below
 		// fades the beam over.
 		effect.life = laserTime_.asFloat();
+		// V4: which texture set the rings are drawn from
+		// (<ringtextureset>, "ring" unless a mod says otherwise). The same
+		// field the explosion events carry their set in, and unused by a
+		// beam until now.
+		effect.texture = params_->getRingTexture();
 		ScorchDroidEffects::push(effect);
 	}
 #endif
